00:10:55,320 --> 00:10:57,360
- Are you hungry?
- If you have some food, take it out.

243
00:10:57,440 --> 00:10:58,440
I’m really glad.

244
00:11:03,200 --> 00:11:04,760
Hi, do you know who I am?

245
00:11:04,920 --> 00:11:07,040
My daughter. Paca.

246
00:11:07,400 --> 00:11:09,680
Good, how are you?

247
00:11:10,680 --> 00:11:11,840
I’m a mess.

248
00:11:13,280 --> 00:11:16,040
- Whose house is this?
- It’s yours, mom.

249
00:11:16,120 --> 00:11:19,200
Sometimes she gets a bit confused.
But she’s really well.

250
00:11:19,640 --> 00:11:20,840
We are.

251
00:11:21,080 --> 00:11:22,440
Right, Fina?

252
00:11:23,320 --> 00:11:25,920
Well, come here.
Sit down and tell me.

253
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:29,720
What are you doing here?
You didn’t call nor wrote.

254
00:11:29,800 --> 00:11:31,840
Will you stay the night?
It gets cold, want a blanket?

255
00:11:31,960 --> 00:11:35,840
Don’t worry. Don’t lift a finger.
If I decide to stay the night,

256
00:11:36,040 --> 00:11:38,400
I know my way around here. Listen.

257
00:11:38,640 --> 00:11:41,480
Relax and drink your coffee,
I have something to tell you.

258
00:11:41,560 --> 00:11:43,920
- You’re scaring me, Paquita.
- No. Don’t worry.

259
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:45,280
It’s good news.

260
00:11:45,360 --> 00:11:46,640
I was going to call you,

261
00:11:47,080 --> 00:11:49,960
but the trip was worth the news.

262
00:11:50,040 --> 00:11:53,840
- All right.
- I was at the office this morning,

263
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:55,920
Chos called me

264
00:11:56,360 --> 00:11:57,880
and said...

265
00:11:58,640 --> 00:12:00,600
that you were picked for a series.

266
00:12:01,680 --> 00:12:03,520
I still don’t have the scripts
or anything,

267
00:12:03,600 --> 00:12:06,400
but they want you,
no need for a casting.

268
00:12:06,480 --> 00:12:08,240
- A TV series?
- Of course.

269
00:12:08,720 --> 00:12:09,960
The leading role.

270
00:12:10,160 --> 00:12:12,840
Clara, we’ll be back.

271
00:12:14,320 --> 00:12:15,400
Back.

272
00:12:17,640 --> 00:12:18,680
I...

273
00:12:24,760 --> 00:12:25,600
Clara...

274
00:12:27,400 --> 00:12:28,560
Clara...

275
00:12:29,400 --> 00:12:30,800
- Clara, are you okay?
-I...

276
00:12:31,120 --> 00:12:33,520
Excuse me, Paquita,
I’ll lay down for a minute.

277
00:12:35,800 --> 00:12:36,840
With Clara?

278
00:12:37,240 --> 00:12:41,320
With her...
We followed a bit risky strategy.

279
00:12:44,760 --> 00:12:48,520
We photoshopped her face
in another actress’ pictures.

280
00:12:48,720 --> 00:12:51,840
Her at The Oscars, on a film set...

281
00:12:51,960 --> 00:12:55,760
advertising shampoo...
Things like that. Very simple.

282
00:12:55,840 --> 00:12:58,040
We had to twist the facts a little.

283
00:12:58,120 --> 00:13:00,000
She was already doing castings
in English,

284
00:13:00,080 --> 00:13:02,760
she was working
and she was getting a lot of callings.

285
00:13:02,840 --> 00:13:05,440
"Why don’t we say
that you’re already part of a project?"

286
00:13:05,520 --> 00:13:09,600
I’ve just returned from Los Angeles,
so I’m still a bit jetlagged.

287
00:13:09,680 --> 00:13:12,040
But very happy because I'm doing

288
00:13:12,120 --> 00:13:15,280
a series named "House of Cards",
maybe you know it.

289
00:13:15,360 --> 00:13:18,680
"House of Cards"...
I didn’t know it was popular in Spain.

290
00:13:18,760 --> 00:13:22,360
We said she did a cameo
in an episode, a small thing.

291
00:13:22,640 --> 00:13:23,800
And they caught us.

292
00:13:24,240 --> 00:13:27,960
They did. The press went crazy.
They called her a liar...

293
00:13:28,200 --> 00:13:29,480
A fraud...

294
00:13:29,760 --> 00:13:31,080
A fake.

295
00:13:31,480 --> 00:13:34,840
She got a bit sensitive,
so I brought her here.

296
00:13:34,960 --> 00:13:36,600
She’s here in Navarrete.

297
00:13:39,440 --> 00:13:40,520
Clara.

298
00:13:44,240 --> 00:13:45,520
Clara, are you okay?

299
00:13:47,400 --> 00:13:49,320
Listen, I’ve got an email from Chos.

300
00:13:50,160 --> 00:13:52,560
Jon González is in the series cast.

301
00:13:54,160 --> 00:13:55,120
Clara.

302
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:57,200
It’s a thriller.

303
00:14:01,840 --> 00:14:03,960
First sequence: your face.

304
00:14:04,240 --> 00:14:05,800
A gun to your head.

305
00:14:06,240 --> 00:14:07,360
Clara.

306
00:14:17,840 --> 00:14:18,840
Bye.

307
00:14:20,760 --> 00:14:22,160
- Hello.
- Hi.

308
00:14:22,720 --> 00:14:23,960
I’m visiting.

309
00:14:24,040 --> 00:14:25,400
- How come?
- Well, you know...

310
00:14:25,480 --> 00:14:27,520
-That's great.
- I'm only here for the day.

311
00:14:27,600 --> 00:14:29,480
- Glad to see you.
-Me too.

312
00:14:31,080 --> 00:14:33,040
- Hi.
- I’ve got Macarena.

313
00:14:33,280 --> 00:14:35,160
That’s Macarena!

314
00:14:35,520 --> 00:14:36,840
Yes, that’s her.

315
00:15:19,080 --> 00:15:21,280
- Hello, Arturo.
- Good night, Paquita.

316
00:15:21,360 --> 00:15:23,840
- How are you?
- Fine, are you in the hood?

317
00:15:23,920 --> 00:15:26,680
- Yeah, I’m visiting.
- That’s good, what can I get you?

318
00:15:26,760 --> 00:15:29,120
A Gin-tonic and some fried bacon.

319
00:15:29,200 --> 00:15:30,560
Good, well fried, right?

320
00:15:30,640 --> 00:15:32,400
- Like always.
- You haven’t changed.

321
00:15:32,960 --> 00:15:35,480
Your drink is on me.

322
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:37,320
Thanks, Pepe.

323
00:15:37,560 --> 00:15:40,720
What’s wrong, Paqui?
You don’t want to mingle with the poor?

324
00:15:41,400 --> 00:15:44,320
Right, now you play in first division.

325
00:15:44,520 --> 00:15:47,160
They already told me
that you’re training a soccer team.

326
00:15:47,240 --> 00:15:49,080
Yeah, I’m still here in the town.

327
00:15:49,560 --> 00:15:51,120
I haven’t forgotten you tho.

328
00:15:51,200 --> 00:15:54,280
If the streets could talk...

329
00:15:54,840 --> 00:15:56,800
Even if I play in first division,

330
00:15:57,560 --> 00:16:01,040
I still do friendly matches.

331
00:16:01,360 --> 00:16:05,560
I am willing to play
a friendly match, even extra time.

332
00:16:11,080 --> 00:16:13,440
- I can't reach.
- There, there.

333
00:16:15,360 --> 00:16:16,880
- They're very expensive.
- Shh! Hush!

334
00:16:37,320 --> 00:16:38,480
Paquita.

335
00:16:39,760 --> 00:16:40,840
It’s me.

336
00:16:41,680 --> 00:16:42,680
Hi.

337
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:45,680
- Good morning.
- Where are my glasses?

338
00:16:49,520 --> 00:16:50,840
Here. I brought you some tea.

339
00:16:51,240 --> 00:16:53,080
What time is it?
My cell phone died.

340
00:16:53,160 --> 00:16:54,200
8 a.m.

341
00:17:04,040 --> 00:17:05,040
Paquita,

342
00:17:05,640 --> 00:17:07,920
I’m sorry if I scared you yesterday,

343
00:17:09,160 --> 00:17:10,760
but I’ve been thinking

344
00:17:12,560 --> 00:17:14,160
and I don’t want to do it.

345
00:17:15,240 --> 00:17:18,200
It’s a chapter of my life
that I already closed and...

346
00:17:18,800 --> 00:17:20,320
I don’t want to open it again.

347
00:17:21,680 --> 00:17:24,440
Clara, it’s a great opportunity.

348
00:17:24,960 --> 00:17:26,920
I know, but I’m good here.

349
00:17:28,680 --> 00:17:31,960
I take care of your mother
and we play a lot of things.

350
00:17:32,040 --> 00:17:34,760
Domino, "currumi"...

351
00:17:34,840 --> 00:17:36,680
- Rummikub.
- Rummikub.

352
00:17:37,520 --> 00:17:39,040
I’m really happy here.

353
00:17:40,480 --> 00:17:43,000
What will you do here
with so much talent?

354
00:17:44,400 --> 00:17:45,840
A lot.

355
00:17:46,520 --> 00:17:49,080
I’m giving a theater workshop for kids.

356
00:17:49,200 --> 00:17:50,560
And some of them...

357
00:17:50,920 --> 00:17:52,480
Well, they’re amazing.

358
00:17:53,040 --> 00:17:54,640
I’m really happy.

359
00:18:00,760 --> 00:18:02,000
Are you sure?

360
00:18:08,600 --> 00:18:09,720
I am.

361
00:18:13,360 --> 00:18:14,360
All right.

362
00:18:16,240 --> 00:18:18,120
- Thanks.
- No, thank you.

363
00:18:28,800 --> 00:18:30,280
Can I tell you something?

364
00:18:31,400 --> 00:18:32,360
What?

365
00:18:34,160 --> 00:18:36,240
Wanna know what I told
the kids the other day?

366
00:18:37,560 --> 00:18:39,560
That I did a movie in Hollywood.

367
00:18:40,560 --> 00:18:41,640
God, Clara...

368
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:44,080
I don’t know why I did it,
maybe out of habit.

369
00:18:44,160 --> 00:18:45,840
I used to say that a lot...

370
00:18:49,680 --> 00:18:52,200
I’m serious, you should have seen
their faces.

371
00:18:54,720 --> 00:18:56,680
They looked at me as if I was a star.

372
00:19:06,520 --> 00:19:08,080
It’s very hard to wish

373
00:19:10,840 --> 00:19:12,840
for something so coveted.

374
00:19:14,480 --> 00:19:15,560
Very hard.

375
00:19:16,480 --> 00:19:17,760
Clarita...

376
00:19:21,840 --> 00:19:26,040
If we had done it better,
we would have gotten so far...

377
00:19:28,240 --> 00:19:29,280
Well...

378
00:19:30,520 --> 00:19:32,000
We got to Navarrete.

379
00:19:33,840 --> 00:19:35,080
You’re right.

380
00:19:42,120 --> 00:19:44,360
- I love you, Paquita.
- Me too.

381
00:19:48,680 --> 00:19:50,200
Well, I should go.

382
00:19:50,840 --> 00:19:52,960
Mom, give me a kiss.

383
00:19:53,840 --> 00:19:56,840
I’ll die and you won’t be here.
I’ll die alone.

384
00:19:56,920 --> 00:19:58,920
Don’t say nonsense.

385
00:19:59,400 --> 00:20:01,360
Clara is here,
she treats you like a queen.

386
00:20:02,160 --> 00:20:04,800
- She misses you a lot, Paca.
- I know, I do too.

387
00:20:04,920 --> 00:20:08,240
But I’m very busy with actors,
actresses, TV...

388
00:20:09,400 --> 00:20:10,800
I love TV.

389
00:20:12,800 --> 00:20:14,160
You can imagine...

390
00:20:14,240 --> 00:20:16,760
that I’m the one behind all of that
every time you watch it.

391
00:20:18,920 --> 00:20:20,720
<i>You don’t want anybody, bitch</i>!

392
00:20:20,800 --> 00:20:22,160
<i>- Do you know what I want</i>?
<i>- What</i>!

393
00:20:22,240 --> 00:20:23,280
<i>- Do you</i>?
<i>- What</i>!

394
00:20:23,360 --> 00:20:25,240
<i>- This</i>!
<i>- Damn</i>.

395
00:20:26,200 --> 00:20:29,520
- Well, I have to go.
- Here, I packed some food for you.

396
00:20:29,600 --> 00:20:30,680
Food?

397
00:20:30,760 --> 00:20:34,280
They are croquettes, pasties...
A little bit of everything.

398
00:20:34,360 --> 00:20:35,440
Really?

399
00:20:35,520 --> 00:20:38,480
- Yeah, now I cook and everything.
- All right, I’ll get going.

400
00:20:39,040 --> 00:20:40,320
Goodbye.

401
00:20:45,160 --> 00:20:46,720
- Bye, Paquita.
- Don’t come out.

402
00:20:46,800 --> 00:20:48,600
Come on, you’ll catch a cold.

403
00:20:48,680 --> 00:20:50,920
- Drive safe, okay?
- Yeah, don’t worry.

404
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:53,200
- Be careful.
- God, I’m an experienced driver.

405
00:20:53,280 --> 00:20:55,280
Paquita! Paquita! Paquita!

406
00:20:56,200 --> 00:20:57,400
What?

407
00:20:57,960 --> 00:20:59,480
Take me to Madrid.

408
00:20:59,840 --> 00:21:02,160
- What for?
- I want to be an artist.

409
00:21:02,240 --> 00:21:03,840
Really?
What’s your talent?

410
00:21:03,920 --> 00:21:05,560
- Dancing.
- Dancing?

411
00:21:05,640 --> 00:21:06,760
Show me.

412
00:21:26,440 --> 00:21:27,640
Very good!

413
00:21:27,800 --> 00:21:28,960
Come here.

414
00:21:29,520 --> 00:21:33,200
Let’s do something.
When you’re a bit older, call me.

415
00:21:33,560 --> 00:21:35,400
Come to Madrid
and I’ll be your manager, okay?

416
00:21:35,480 --> 00:21:37,680
- I’ll make you a star.
- Hurray!

417
00:21:38,040 --> 00:21:40,240
- Give me a hug.
- Thanks, Paquita.

418
00:21:40,480 --> 00:21:41,720
Thank you, Sonia.

419
00:21:43,760 --> 00:21:45,560
- Bye.
- See you.

420
00:21:47,520 --> 00:21:48,720
Charo...

421
00:21:49,600 --> 00:21:51,680
- Come back soon.
- On Christmas.

